[[:db/retract 17592186124889 :question/answer-fields 17592186122356] {:db/id "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/548d7946665dbb2916800e237d314d924b4f0b8a18672933790f536eff1af851" :answer/id #uuid "0f7e761c-b7b1-5be7-9763-fc045c427922" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨2,0,1⟩+t\\,⟨2,0,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/d0410768e822e5d2210f67fb0eec61786ab9d95f7bc50ec92c95ba96e75e36b0" :answer/id #uuid "023f29d5-82cf-5948-829c-6302657e2ae2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨2,0,1⟩+t\\,⟨1,0,-2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/5377151c024f3dd09f2d730a5e9f535fd7c090f64382250b40ffe19b7f5367e6" :answer/id #uuid "f03332fd-f333-53d5-983b-f10658ee30dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+t\\,⟨2,0,1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/9743c4f05fe7229aa55670016e20efb23aeaf6b4bcbf8083ab17d261360c4060" :answer/id #uuid "1aa8707f-8700-5051-aa22-9156a8241454" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨2,0,1⟩+t\\,⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/75de9ea8564e4a44001fd3e3ceda0eda0937e53fce3d55afc490a4fac56fb662" :answer/id #uuid "b602dbc4-d5ff-56e6-a31e-4023f06f2940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+t\\,⟨1,0,-2⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e" :answer-field/id #uuid "35cd2797-c353-5537-b4ab-9e223730385f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/d0410768e822e5d2210f67fb0eec61786ab9d95f7bc50ec92c95ba96e75e36b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/548d7946665dbb2916800e237d314d924b4f0b8a18672933790f536eff1af851" "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/d0410768e822e5d2210f67fb0eec61786ab9d95f7bc50ec92c95ba96e75e36b0" "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/5377151c024f3dd09f2d730a5e9f535fd7c090f64382250b40ffe19b7f5367e6" "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/9743c4f05fe7229aa55670016e20efb23aeaf6b4bcbf8083ab17d261360c4060" "q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e/75de9ea8564e4a44001fd3e3ceda0eda0937e53fce3d55afc490a4fac56fb662"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36343"] :question/problem "Find a vector equation of the normal line to the surface $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ at the point $(2,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$ \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(2,0,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,0,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(2,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2})j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2}-{z}^{2})k \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}\\text{ }i-2y\\text{ }j-2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(2,0,1) & =\\frac{(2)}{2}\\,i-2(0)\\text{ }j-2(1)\\,k \\\\  & =i-2\\,k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the vector equation of the line that is parallel to $∇f(2,0,1)$ and passes through the point $(2,0,1)$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨2,0,1⟩+t\\,∇f(2,0,1)=⟨2,0,1⟩+t\\,⟨1,0,-2⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/answer-fields ["q-36343/selection/ma-v1/a20d4966519cc3dc9bfd9fd44370d079bc1bb3ec9c5aca0e96df379a890c005e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-37570"] :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)=xy+5x+{z}^{2}$, find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,2)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,-1,2).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+5x+{z}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy+5x+{z}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy+5x+{z}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(y+5)\\text{ }i+x\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(1,-1,2) & =(-1+5)\\,i+(1)\\,j+2(2)\\,k \\\\  & =4\\,i+j+4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4\\,i+j+4\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-1,2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-71390/selection/2637f8fabed2009258545a634746aeaf9ebbf1a91c1a5af01b6e54e78ec289ce" :answer/id #uuid "cdb075fa-2d0a-5255-94bd-b4fffad59a63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3y+2x+11=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71390/selection/a79fd0fe06b380539c9cb7176421a7f5b2732ff7b2f0f1f14ae37a842c8485f0" :answer/id #uuid "c052da68-9376-5e50-8260-0281f8ffc882" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3y+x+10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71390/selection/1e0e5f0fbed7fccc4d117fc2e4727279fbefe82f3f4ec323a3dc4428f6ad6128" :answer/id #uuid "8f7b5da4-db4d-5be4-a55c-3640fa3a50df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y+3x+4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71390/selection/279c954c83de0dc7f60daede71b9b88ae7bbf392b3a226f89221b964c1f47dbf" :answer/id #uuid "7c421a59-b128-5931-a3f9-d010cac8075c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y+3x+20=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71390/selection/d537feaba10bef5b08a909f9f0a4a506752298ed26737e4017ff42a99dce1c99" :answer/id #uuid "869fad40-a9aa-5e3e-b0de-cfbdc7e800fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3y-x+8=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71390/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "309f94ed-f121-5109-b3ec-c8f09f8031bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71390/selection/a79fd0fe06b380539c9cb7176421a7f5b2732ff7b2f0f1f14ae37a842c8485f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-71390/selection/2637f8fabed2009258545a634746aeaf9ebbf1a91c1a5af01b6e54e78ec289ce" "q-71390/selection/a79fd0fe06b380539c9cb7176421a7f5b2732ff7b2f0f1f14ae37a842c8485f0" "q-71390/selection/1e0e5f0fbed7fccc4d117fc2e4727279fbefe82f3f4ec323a3dc4428f6ad6128" "q-71390/selection/279c954c83de0dc7f60daede71b9b88ae7bbf392b3a226f89221b964c1f47dbf" "q-71390/selection/d537feaba10bef5b08a909f9f0a4a506752298ed26737e4017ff42a99dce1c99"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71390" :question/id #uuid "638e57db-1875-5145-9276-ae3c006b2add" :question/math-academy-id "q-71390" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve ${y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}=4xy.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(-1,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}+3{x}^{2} & =4xy \\\\ {y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4xy & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4xy$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(-1,-3)$ can be found by computing $∇f(-1,-3).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(-1,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4xy)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+3{x}^{2}-4xy)\\,j \\\\  & =(6x-4y)\\,i+(2y-4x)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-1,-3) & =(6(-1)-4(-3))\\,i+(2(-3)-4(-1))\\,j \\\\  & =6\\,i-2\\,j \\\\  & =⟨6,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(-1,-3)=⟨6,-2⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(-1,-3).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(-1)}{6} & =\\frac{y-(-3)}{-2} \\\\ (-2)(x+1) & =6(y+3) \\\\ -2x-2 & =6y+18 \\\\ 6y+2x+20 & =0 \\\\ 3y+x+10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71390/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2f7fab-cebe-519a-83e3-a0831cac289d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71390"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71399/selection/39985d70ab4dfc808aa1f5d35d6745e4a01934de0e02ce0c162419cb6ed06f7b" :answer/id #uuid "0164703a-ec17-5af3-8556-253210803cf1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71399/selection/6c0cf2e3db20a0bea079d3658ec5b4df2ccf15a94420b1c5738af55d521bf260" :answer/id #uuid "1331d0de-213c-5c14-86f3-99ba20c0e581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i+j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71399/selection/c1dce1f2a3d4009077e0c813dd56fd73b6c9f74650457c5a083f9a0b429122da" :answer/id #uuid "64fdab4b-e75c-5bd4-ad03-1a21854d4266" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+2\\,j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71399/selection/65804235d7bb4b17b7f416e60a2e70b14da5e8ccdcf4ea5163765c822cba76d5" :answer/id #uuid "3a78c73e-0e82-5624-9902-3c12c12a1378" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i+2\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71399/selection/fc3cf9a9c9d0f107d15f4c431948eb277ad3e5d7c87f47ffc2e9cd7858d13f7d" :answer/id #uuid "d8a39959-6f6b-5567-b32a-ff76d465962f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i+j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71399/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9551214e-3aef-5928-95ca-04325962387f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71399/selection/39985d70ab4dfc808aa1f5d35d6745e4a01934de0e02ce0c162419cb6ed06f7b" :answer-field/choices ["q-71399/selection/39985d70ab4dfc808aa1f5d35d6745e4a01934de0e02ce0c162419cb6ed06f7b" "q-71399/selection/6c0cf2e3db20a0bea079d3658ec5b4df2ccf15a94420b1c5738af55d521bf260" "q-71399/selection/c1dce1f2a3d4009077e0c813dd56fd73b6c9f74650457c5a083f9a0b429122da" "q-71399/selection/65804235d7bb4b17b7f416e60a2e70b14da5e8ccdcf4ea5163765c822cba76d5" "q-71399/selection/fc3cf9a9c9d0f107d15f4c431948eb277ad3e5d7c87f47ffc2e9cd7858d13f7d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71399" :question/id #uuid "58a67c4a-aa8b-5b64-8268-56928e2716de" :question/math-academy-id "q-71399" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={e}^{x+y+z}+x+y+z$, find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(0,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(0,0,0)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(0,0,0).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(0,0,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{x+y+z}+x+y+z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{x+y+z}+x+y+z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{x+y+z}+x+y+z)\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{x+y+z}+1)\\text{ }i+({e}^{x+y+z}+1)\\text{ }j+({e}^{x+y+z}+1)\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(0,0,0) & =({e}^{0+0+0}+1)\\,i+({e}^{0+0+0}+1)\\,j+({e}^{0+0+0}+1)\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2\\,i+2\\,j+2\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(0,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71399/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4516cb28-0fc0-5c15-b9b2-747c3827e189"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71399"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130723/selection/fc87bf7d9541507db69be45cb8dbb13e79c8cda578ffc266ead942a6e1a22462" :answer/id #uuid "349dd0d4-2103-5d58-9d70-5684f7d1c25b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2y-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130723/selection/f686ff10a645319189dba94c562df0382ee16e2b8eaaf31989ecb45c5d1c8a75" :answer/id #uuid "521b35cb-272d-5f5f-9362-e2979add7a0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-y-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130723/selection/aafcb3e5284b08d0e7601c8ebd533ff879625d8dfad810badf24d1a1cbc643a2" :answer/id #uuid "dcd8e553-85cc-5d4e-8c79-263f403f59a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y-1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130723/selection/63ea1ec99195bcb3eeb1ce7ab8b8d8bf5514f9f358a4384b4c63d04b47b01f85" :answer/id #uuid "2a4ed07b-fd19-5354-a343-1270af930046" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130723/selection/3640b3008c0c62ef413f3c2ce6865dde48c221f43f0778da5cdce5d870a034e7" :answer/id #uuid "98148e5b-8268-5ccc-831f-115348d84820" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-3y-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130723/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4815db71-8cf2-513a-a965-c49db07b416a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130723/selection/f686ff10a645319189dba94c562df0382ee16e2b8eaaf31989ecb45c5d1c8a75" :answer-field/choices ["q-130723/selection/fc87bf7d9541507db69be45cb8dbb13e79c8cda578ffc266ead942a6e1a22462" "q-130723/selection/f686ff10a645319189dba94c562df0382ee16e2b8eaaf31989ecb45c5d1c8a75" "q-130723/selection/aafcb3e5284b08d0e7601c8ebd533ff879625d8dfad810badf24d1a1cbc643a2" "q-130723/selection/63ea1ec99195bcb3eeb1ce7ab8b8d8bf5514f9f358a4384b4c63d04b47b01f85" "q-130723/selection/3640b3008c0c62ef413f3c2ce6865dde48c221f43f0778da5cdce5d870a034e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130723" :question/id #uuid "ce165faf-65bc-55f7-97d6-2084afaa6bca" :question/math-academy-id "q-130723" :question/problem "Consider the plane curve $4xy+2{x}^{2}=x+2y.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4xy+2{x}^{2} & =x+2y \\\\ 4xy+2{x}^{2}-x-2y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=4xy+2{x}^{2}-x-2y$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$   \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(2,-1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(2,-1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4xy+2{x}^{2}-x-2y)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4xy+2{x}^{2}-x-2y)\\,j \\\\  & =(4y+4x-1)\\,i+(4x-2)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-1) & =(4(-1)+4(2)-1)\\,i+(4(2)-2)\\,j \\\\  & =3\\,i+6\\,j \\\\  & =⟨3,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Hence, $∇f(2,-1)=⟨3,6⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(2,-1).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}} & =\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}} \\\\ \\frac{x-2}{3} & =\\frac{y-(-1)}{6} \\\\ 6(x-2) & =3(y+1) \\\\ 2(x-2) & =y+1 \\\\ 2x-4 & =y+1 \\\\ 2x-y-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130723/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2f7fab-cebe-519a-83e3-a0831cac289d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130723"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
